{
  "about": "Mock AMM (step 4.D) constant-product vectors, computed by hand with integer arithmetic (checked with Python's int, never with the Rust code). fee_in = ceil(amount_in * fee_bps / 10000); a = amount_in - fee_in; amount_out = floor(a * r_out / (r_in + a)); gross_out = floor(amount_in * r_out / (r_in + amount_in)); fee_out = gross_out - amount_out (the fee in output tokens, the desk's /swap-quote fee_u); min_out = floor(amount_out * (10000 - slippage_bps) / 10000). amount_out 0 means the program refuses the swap (ZeroOut). Used by programs/mock-amm/tests (LiteSVM), crates/desk/src/swap (quote math) and app/tx (swap instruction).",
  "fee_bps": 50,
  "slippage_bps": 50,
